# Nested/external clones should be added as proper submodules if needed.
Github/

# PPD full-database downloads. Third-party dumps, redownloadable from
# publicplansdata.org, ~9 MB. The .xlsx form is already covered above; this
# catches the .csv form. The small hand-curated PPD_planlevel_main*.csv files
# are model inputs and stay tracked.
Data/**/ppd-data-latest.csv
Data/**/ppd-data-*.csv

# Derived analysis cache. Reduces every scenario run to per-plan exhaustion curves
# so the notebook opens in seconds instead of ~25 minutes. Regenerable from the runs
# themselves; delete it after a new run to force a rebuild.
Analysis/output/exhibit_cache.pkl

# Brookings BPEA 2021 replication package (their Data & Programs zip, extracted).
# Third-party data, ~11 MB, re-downloadable from the article page:
#   brookings.edu/articles/the-sustainability-of-state-and-local-government-pensions-...
# Ignored for two reasons: it is data, which this repo does not track, and its nested
# paths exceed the Windows path limit under the OneDrive folder name, so git cannot
# index them at all. Where to get it and what is in it: Documentation + the crosswalk
# cell at the top of Analysis/results.ipynb.
Data/Sources/brookings_bpea2021_replication/
